      "message": "sitive_attempt_2/downstream.py`.\n\n**What it contains**\n- `CONTRACT_VERSION = 2` \u2014 the version observed in `committed/A_direct/producer.py` (v2, not the v1 the first B attempt may have assumed), preserved as a module-level constant plus a runtime guard in `consume`.\n- `_idempotency_key_fallback(request)` \u2014 a verbatim copied equivalent of the upstream semantics: `request['id'] + ':' + request.get('attempt', '0')`, i.e. retries of the same id are *not* collapsed (`'A:1'` \u2260 `'A:0'`).\n- `_producer_idempotency_key()` \u2014 resolves the producer function by importing `producer` / `committed.A_direct.producer` when reachable, otherwise falls back to the copied implementation. No import of `semkg_contract`.\n- `consume(value)` \u2014 calls the producer function (or the equivalent copy) and returns the key.\n\n**Local check**\n`CONTRACT_VERSION=2`; `consume({'id':'A','attempt':'2'})=='A:2'`, `consume({'id':'B'})=='B:0'`, `consume({'id':'A','attempt':'1'})=='A:1'`; `'semkg_contract' in sys.modules` \u2192 `False`."
